{#- The drawer (X11, Batch X; first shipped as V11's labels drawer). ONE
    partial, driven entirely by _data/labels.js: for this page, a title,
    THE RULES (left column, a bullet list) and THE LABELS (right column, the
    confidence-table style: chip | what it tells you).

    C1 (sweep 2026-10-10): it is an always-open section, not a collapsible
    <details>. The title is a real heading (h2.ldrawer-title, at the footer
    "Get updates" heading's size), the h3s "The rules" / "The labels" sit
    under it, and the whole section is --white with the 4px coral rule on its
    top edge (integration.css item 116). The name "drawer" is kept for the
    class, the data-screen-label and the build guard; nothing opens or closes.

    A label with no approved definition yet renders its chip only. Where no
    label on the page has one, the table drops its second column rather than
    showing an empty one — nothing is invented to fill it.

    A page with no entry in labels.js renders nothing. -#}
{%- set drawer = labels.pages[page.url] %}
{%- if drawer %}
{%- set lh = labels.headings %}
<section class="ldrawer" id="{{ drawer.id }}" data-screen-label="Drawer">
  <h2 class="ldrawer-title">{{ drawer.summary }}</h2>
  <div class="ldrawer-body">
    <div class="ldrawer-rules">
      <h3>{{ lh.rules }}</h3>
      <ul>
{%- for rule in drawer.rules %}
        <li>{{ rule }}</li>
{%- endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="ldrawer-labels">
      <h3>{{ lh.labels }}</h3>
      <table class="conftable">
        <thead><tr><th>{{ lh.label }}</th>{% if drawer.hasDefinitions %}<th>{{ lh.meaning }}</th>{% endif %}</tr></thead>
        <tbody>
{%- for name in drawer.labels %}
{%- set l = labels.labels[name] %}
          <tr data-label="{{ name }}"><td><span class="{{ l.chip }}">{{ name }}</span></td>{% if drawer.hasDefinitions %}<td>{{ l.definition or "" }}</td>{% endif %}</tr>
{%- endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
{%- if drawer.elsewhere %}
{%- for name, where in drawer.elsewhere %}
      <p class="ldrawer-note" data-label-note="{{ name }}">{{ lh.usedOn }} <a href="{{ where.href }}">{{ where.name }}</a>.</p>
{%- endfor %}
{%- endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif %}
